  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Children and Young People&#x2019;s Taskforce (ODA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">o implement the meaningful participation of children and young people into the Global Care Reform Campaign, we are establishing an International Taskforce of Children and Young People aged 14-25 with child rights organisations (Able Child, Hope and Homes for Children, Save the Children, and World Vision). The Taskforce will serve as a participatory advisory body to the Global Care Reform Campaign. Through the Taskforce, we aim to ensure meaningful and inclusive participation of children and young people with lived experience of being outside parental care (for example, of family separation and different forms of alternative care) or experience of the child protection system (for example, those at risk of family separation). The aim of this is to bring diverse voices and lived experience into the Campaign to shape its development, implementation and campaign-level accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
